{"text": " What are tariffs? Monkeys live in two countries, Monkey Land and Banana Land. Monkey Land has many monkey, but not many banana. Banana Land has many banana, but not many monkey. Monkey Land monkeys need more banana, and since Banana Land grows so many, they can sell them for cheap. So Monkey Land buy banana from Banana Land. When Monkey Country buy thing from other Monkey Country, this is called importing. When a Monkey Country sells something to other Monkey Country, this is called exporting. Banana Land monkeys make money. Monkey Land monkeys get banana for cheap. Monkey's happy. Monkey's friends. Life good. Monkey Land government put tariff on all bananas from Banana Land. A tariff is a tax, an extra charge to bring banana from Banana Land into Monkey Land. When Monkey get food delivered, Monkey pay for food, Monkey pay for delivery, a tariff is like the service fee.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 1.72, "text": " What are tariffs?", "tokens": [50363, 1867, 389, 29240, 30, 50449], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16539329339650052, "compression_ratio": 2.253393665158371, "no_speech_prob": 0.01032677385956049}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 1.72, "end": 5.08, "text": " Monkeys live in two countries, Monkey Land and Banana Land.", "tokens": [50449, 2892, 13083, 2107, 287, 734, 2678, 11, 26997, 6379, 290, 40058, 6379, 13, 50617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16539329339650052, "compression_ratio": 2.253393665158371, "no_speech_prob": 0.01032677385956049}, {"id": 2, "seek": 0, "start": 5.08, "end": 8.52, "text": " Monkey Land has many monkey, but not many banana.", "tokens": [50617, 26997, 6379, 468, 867, 21657, 11, 475, 407, 867, 25996, 13, 50789], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16539329339650052, "compression_ratio": 2.253393665158371, "no_speech_prob": 0.01032677385956049}, {"id": 3, "seek": 0, "start": 8.52, "end": 11.24, "text": " Banana Land has many banana, but not many monkey.", "tokens": [50789, 40058,